{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/t0zux47q","slide":2,"text":"Ask of every loop: are the iterations strangers to each other?","textPreview":"Ask of every loop: are the iterations strangers to each other?","textChars":62,"textLines":1,"bbox":[58,674,1164,28]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/aib2md","slide":2,"text":"The model was present before CUDA: every pixel was already decided independently. Section 4 showed floats disguised as colors and matrices as textures. Brook named the stream-and-kernel abstraction; CUDA removed the graphics disguise and made it native. Data-parallel code often ports naturally. Deeply serial code must be rethought rather than translated."}
