{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/butsbm9s","slide":3,"text":"The library is the contract that can outlive the hardware.","textPreview":"The library is the contract that can outlive the hardware.","textChars":58,"textLines":1,"bbox":[58,674,1164,28]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/1v1u9w","slide":3,"text":"NVIDIA's integrated stack—CUDA plus tuned libraries—became part of the product. Vendor libraries are rewritten for each architecture and are the usual path to specialized units such as tensor cores. On common operations, hand-written kernels often lose to vendor libraries and may age worse across hardware generations. Do not make the claim absolute: custom kernels remain important for fusion, unusual operations, and the glue between library calls."}
