{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/mtsvydcf","slide":5,"text":"Choose precision deliberately—and check what the actual card provides.","textPreview":"Choose precision deliberately—and check what the actual card provides.","textChars":70,"textLines":1,"bbox":[58,674,1164,28]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/tzs1t2","slide":5,"text":"First, every launch has overhead. The structural remedies are batching, fusion, and capture/replay for repeated sequences. Second, precision is a priced choice. The history showed consumer FP64 deliberately segmented from datacenter FP64, while tensor cores created fast lower-precision paths. Precision also changes data movement: halving width doubles the values carried by the same memory traffic. Avoid treating the displayed formats as a universal ranking; the real device and workload decide."}
